## 🔹 What are HTML Entities?

HTML entities are special codes used to display characters that have a special meaning in HTML or characters that may not be easy to type directly.

### Examples

| Entity     | Output             |
| ---------- | ------------------ |
| `&lt;`     | `<`                |
| `&gt;`     | `>`                |
| `&amp;`    | `&`                |
| `&quot;`   | `"`                |
| `&apos;`   | `'`                |
| `&nbsp;`   | Non-breaking space |
| `&copy;`   | ©                  |
| `&reg;`    | ®                  |
| `&trade;`  | ™                  |
| `&hearts;` | ♥                  |
| `&euro;`   | €                  |
| `&pound;`  | £                  |
| `&yen;`    | ¥                  |
| `&cent;`   | ¢                  |

---

## 🔢 Numeric Character References

HTML entities can also be written using numeric character references.

### Decimal Example

```html
&#169;
```

Output:

©

### Hexadecimal Example

```html
&#xA9;
```

Output:

©

Indian Rupee:

```html
&#8377;
```

Output:

₹

